From 80b545c28dfc8ba68d7d216fd07fb6aeb18200f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:23:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): shell-quote sys.executable wherever it becomes a
 shell word [daveey]

On a Mac whose interpreter lives under a path with a space (~/Applications/Hermes Python.app/...),
command strings built as f"{sys.executable} ..." split at the space and the helper never starts
(exit 127). Tests then fail (the hermes-mods coach process-exit watcher test) or pass hollowly (the
process-consumer health tests launched 0 fixture helpers).

- shlex.quote the interpreter, and the script path beside it, at 12 shell-command sites: 11 test
  fixtures/helpers (hook commands, GIT_EDITOR, wrapper scripts, helper commands) and the Teams
  adapter's pip install hint, the only product site.
- tests/test_shell_quoted_interpreter.py: an AST scan of the repo that fails on a bare
  sys.executable used as a shell command word. Shebangs are exempt (the kernel splits them before
  any shell, so quoting cannot help); argv lists and whole-string uses are fine.

Proof on macOS with the spaced Python 3.14.9 (the guard also on the core venv's 3.11.7):
- guard: parent + guard = 12 offenders (1 failed, 18 passed) on both Pythons; this commit = 19 passed.
- process-consumer health tests: 0 fixture helpers launched before, 17 after (47 passed both ways).
- hermes-mods coach watcher test with this tree on PYTHONPATH: 1 failed before, 51 passed after.
- the 17 affected test files run serially: 24 failed before, 22 after, no new failures. Fixed:
  test_upstream_sync::test_pre_push_guard_refuses_a_hand_pushed_sync_and_allows_fork_work and
  test_served_profile_child_env::test_helper_children_resolve_secrets_through_the_served_profile.
  The 22 that fail both ways contain no quoting site and fail identically on the parent under
  this interpreter.
